        "model": "deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 11,
        "title": "Reddit CAPI first-prompt and retention conversions overhauled",
        "summary": "sendRedditCustomConversion is no longer fire-and-forget: it returns RedditCapiDeliveryResult ('sent'|'disabled') and throws RedditCapiDeliveryError (with status) after a single retry of transient 408/429/5xx failures, gated by IS_PROD or an explicit enabled flag. The event-name model collapses surface-suffixed names into a single RedditCapiEventName union ('FirstPrompt'|'Retention1d'|'Retention7d'|'Retention24d') with REDDIT_FIRST_PROMPT_EVENT defined, and redditConversionId now hashes 'event:userId' with sha256 instead of joining event/userId/timestamp. Retention milestones fire only on the exact calendar-day hit (daysSinceFirstToday === milestone) rather than the first day a threshold is crossed, with the new analytics events FREEBUFF_REDDIT_FUNNEL_FIRST_PROMPT and FREEBUFF_REDDIT_FUNNEL_RETENTION_1D/7D/24D backing the same milestones.",
        "significance": "major",
        "audience": "operators",
        "evidence": "reddit-capi.ts rewrites sendRedditCustomConversion from a fire-and-forget returning Promise<void> into a retrying function returning RedditCapiDeliveryResult ('sent'|'disabled') that retries one transient failure (status 408/429/5xx) with RedditCapiDeliveryError carrying the status; reddit-capi-events.ts replaces surface-suffixed RedditCapiEventName variants (FirstPromptCli, Retention1dCli) with a single union ('FirstPrompt'|'sRetention1d'|'Retention7d'|'Retention24d') and adds REDDIT_FIRST_PROMPT_EVENT; reddit-freebuff-retention.ts changes getFreebuffRetentionMilestonesToFire to fire only on the exact calendar-day milestone (daysSinceFirstToday === milestone) instead of crossing a threshold; analytics-events.ts adds FREEBUFF_REDDIT_FUNNEL_FIRST_PROMPT and retention_1d/7d/24d.",
        "userVisible": false,
        "confidence": "high",
        "unknowns": "The diff shows the shared-core rewrite but not the service-side callers that consume the new return type, the unified event names, or the exact-day retention gating, nor the rollout of the newly added analytics events. A second read of the same diff did not confirm that a migration step is required.",
